WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.500
- I have this drone
pretty much entirely done.

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:06.179
And I've even managed to
bind it to this controller.

00:00:06.179 --> 00:00:09.115
There is some sort of connection.

00:00:09.115 --> 00:00:11.619
But I can't control the motors.

00:00:11.619 --> 00:00:14.536
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:18.672
- It's awesome.

00:00:18.672 --> 00:00:20.035
- [Man] Are they gonna
find some for the rain?

00:00:20.035 --> 00:00:21.802
- It's fine but not for shoes.

00:00:21.802 --> 00:00:23.096
- Today has been a disaster.

00:00:23.096 --> 00:00:24.983
Because it is pouring rain.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:27.973
What I did today was ring a
bunch of racing drone parts

00:00:27.973 --> 00:00:30.229
for this tiny micro drone that I have.

00:00:30.229 --> 00:00:31.975
And I'm going to try to build it

00:00:31.975 --> 00:00:33.745
But we'll see if that actually works.

00:00:33.745 --> 00:00:34.578
It's about this big.

00:00:34.578 --> 00:00:36.265
It's super tiny.

00:00:36.265 --> 00:00:37.479
But the problem is, I've
never actually built a

00:00:37.479 --> 00:00:38.379
racing drone before.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.641
But I bought the parts.

00:00:39.641 --> 00:00:41.605
So hopefully, I can actually
assemble this into something

00:00:41.605 --> 00:00:44.857
that I can race next doorr and
mess with all those people.

00:00:44.857 --> 00:00:45.938
It's a tiny little motor.

00:00:45.938 --> 00:00:47.470
Now we have our control board here.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.986
And this is actually the brains
of the entire drone itself.

00:00:49.986 --> 00:00:51.846
It looks like just any
normal computer chip.

00:00:51.846 --> 00:00:53.676
Except this has its telemetry stuff on it.

00:00:53.676 --> 00:00:55.321
You got a tiny little radio here.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.734
And it will actually power
the motors and the camera.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.276
Look at the size of this thing.

00:01:00.276 --> 00:01:03.144
Here is a nickel right next
to the little FPV camera.

00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:06.445
This is meant to take a real
live video signal from this

00:01:06.445 --> 00:01:10.146
tiny little camera
directly to my eyeballs.

00:01:10.146 --> 00:01:12.111
Woah, Look at all that stuff.

00:01:12.111 --> 00:01:14.293
(machine whirring)

00:01:14.293 --> 00:01:16.379
- Okay, I've never owned an RC boat.

00:01:16.379 --> 00:01:17.628
I've always been jealous.

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:19.561
As a child, I go to friends'
houses and some people would

00:01:19.561 --> 00:01:20.929
have a swimming people.

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:21.924
And, oh, I wish I had a pool.

00:01:21.924 --> 00:01:23.101
And they had an RC Boat.

00:01:23.101 --> 00:01:24.810
They drive it around in their pool.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:25.812
And I was like, "Uhh!"

00:01:25.812 --> 00:01:27.575
The street is completely flooded today.

00:01:27.575 --> 00:01:29.607
And we have these mini
drones leftover from a shoot

00:01:29.607 --> 00:01:33.774
and they have these hydro foils
that should ride on water.

00:01:35.107 --> 00:01:36.456
Do you think it's gonna be deep enough?

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:38.440
- I don't know.

00:01:38.449 --> 00:01:39.956
My feet are wet.

00:01:39.956 --> 00:01:41.309
- I know, this is terrible.

00:01:41.309 --> 00:01:42.142
Look, look at.

00:01:42.142 --> 00:01:43.015
- It's so deep!

00:01:43.015 --> 00:01:44.615
- Look at how much water there is.

00:01:46.852 --> 00:01:48.579
(drone whirring)

00:01:48.579 --> 00:01:49.980
- It's stuck, it's only sitting.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:50.813
- Push it out a bit.

00:01:50.813 --> 00:01:51.646
Okay.

00:01:51.646 --> 00:01:53.364
- Yeah, Yeah, Yeah.

00:01:53.364 --> 00:01:55.614
(shouting)

00:02:00.273 --> 00:02:02.371
It's going, it's going!

00:02:02.371 --> 00:02:04.604
- We gotta, we gotta deepen this thing.

00:02:04.604 --> 00:02:05.998
- Oh my, god.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.380
Oh, no, it's gonna get run over!

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.589
I've started putting this drone together.

00:02:09.589 --> 00:02:11.411
I managed to get the motors
installed in the right spots.

00:02:11.411 --> 00:02:13.794
And I've got the control board
pressed on but I haven't got

00:02:13.794 --> 00:02:16.615
the screws in yet because I
gotta install the camera first.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.507
But my main issue is,
although I know how to solder,

00:02:19.507 --> 00:02:20.632
I'm not particularly good.

00:02:20.632 --> 00:02:22.155
Maybe Spencer can solder this on.

00:02:22.155 --> 00:02:25.023
'Cause what we have to do is
cut the cable for this and

00:02:25.023 --> 00:02:28.467
solder it directly to these
tiny little nodes here.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:32.107
And I don't quite trust
my own skills soldering.

00:02:32.107 --> 00:02:32.999
Soldering skill?

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:33.853
That's the one.

00:02:34.009 --> 00:02:35.010
Should I be bold and just solder it myself

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.781
or should I get Spencer's help?

00:02:36.781 --> 00:02:39.399
My Grandfather's always told me...  Do it!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.500
- I like your grandfather.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.681
I'm gonna do it.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:45.230
(finger taps the table)
I don't need Spencer's help.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:46.113
Little nervous.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.749
First thing's first attaching

00:02:47.749 --> 00:02:50.348
this little FPV camera to the drone.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:51.904
Moment of truth, man.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.118
(Hiphop music)

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.300
According to that image right there,

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.866
red on bottom, black on top.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.786
The red is the power,
the black is the ground.

00:03:02.786 --> 00:03:04.365
- Don't mess up.

00:03:04.365 --> 00:03:06.449
- I will do my best, Nick.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.220
Please work.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:07.880
Please work.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:08.840
Please work.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.843
Aha, I got one on there.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.867
Now to do the other.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:17.340
Did I state that I'm
not very good at this?

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:18.828
(crying)

00:03:18.828 --> 00:03:19.661
Okay, I think I got it.

00:03:19.661 --> 00:03:20.535
I think I got it.

00:03:20.535 --> 00:03:22.610
Just gonna put the liquid tape.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.309
Just a little dab on it.

00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:25.898
You know what electrical tape is?

00:03:25.898 --> 00:03:29.063
This is essentially
that but in liquid form.

00:03:29.063 --> 00:03:29.896
You know what?

00:03:29.896 --> 00:03:30.791
That's good enough.

00:03:30.791 --> 00:03:32.241
Screw it.

00:03:32.241 --> 00:03:33.574
I need a napkin.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:40.254
(cars passing by)

00:03:40.254 --> 00:03:41.108
- Woah, Woah, Woah!

00:03:41.108 --> 00:03:43.025
- Oh my, god, Fuck you!

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:45.813
- Did it die?

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.249
It says it's not connected.

00:03:47.249 --> 00:03:48.232
- I don't think they're waterproof.

00:03:48.232 --> 00:03:49.952
- The drone is now probably dead.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.213
- Did you fulfill your childhood fantasy?

00:03:55.213 --> 00:03:59.210
- Yeah, it was a brief
10 seconds of just glory.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.000
I was on that little boat sailing.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:01.833
5.8 knots.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.575
- Was it worth it?

00:04:03.575 --> 00:04:04.408
- Yes.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.680
(laughing)

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.540
- Play out here, you're
gonna get splashed.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.980
- Why is this so difficult?

00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:21.047
Everything should work.

00:04:21.047 --> 00:04:22.880
Okay, moment of truth.

00:04:23.882 --> 00:04:26.382
(drone beeps)

00:04:27.926 --> 00:04:30.843
(heavy drum music)

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:34.920
Why won't it just work?

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.280
Come on!

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.939
This is so aggravating.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:40.374
I have this drone pretty
much entirely done.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:43.784
And I've even managed to
bind it to this controller.

00:04:43.784 --> 00:04:47.197
So there is some sort of connection.

00:04:47.197 --> 00:04:50.378
But I can't control the motors.

00:04:50.378 --> 00:04:52.845
I just wanna go bug the people next door.

00:04:52.845 --> 00:04:53.678
- In.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:55.853
Out.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.060
- Light is blinking.

00:04:59.291 --> 00:05:00.270
(drone beeps)

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.103
Turn it on.

00:05:01.103 --> 00:05:01.936
Light's on.

00:05:01.936 --> 00:05:04.376
That means it should be connected now.

00:05:06.459 --> 00:05:08.720
The problem I ran into is
that even though I was able

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.279
to bind this to my controller,
I wasn't able to get the

00:05:11.279 --> 00:05:14.149
motors up and running because
there's a setting that

00:05:14.149 --> 00:05:15.491
I didn't actually activate.

00:05:15.491 --> 00:05:18.055
It seems obvious in hindsight
but I didn't have a switch

00:05:18.055 --> 00:05:19.888
set to arm the motors.

00:05:20.836 --> 00:05:21.888
I've now set that switch.

00:05:21.888 --> 00:05:23.688
So now, the thing works.

00:05:24.464 --> 00:05:28.186
It's weird to, like,
walk around like this.

00:05:28.186 --> 00:05:29.019
See, okay.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.259
Here I can walk around just fine.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.700
(Wren grunts)

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.020
(Nick laughs)

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.809
- Let's see a third
person video game to you.

00:05:36.193 --> 00:05:38.860
(electro music)

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.317
This is so weird.

00:05:49.764 --> 00:05:51.800
(Wren laughs)

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:53.366
(sneezes)

00:05:53.366 --> 00:05:54.199
Okay.

00:05:58.667 --> 00:05:59.918
All right.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.240
Maiden flight here in the studio.

00:06:02.797 --> 00:06:05.341
(drone buzzing)

00:06:05.341 --> 00:06:06.174
Woah.

00:06:06.174 --> 00:06:07.007
Woah.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.360
This is not easy to fly, by the way.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.040
Oh, hey, I'm coming up to say hi.

00:06:15.749 --> 00:06:18.482
(drone buzzes)

00:06:18.482 --> 00:06:19.676
Hey, Jake!

00:06:19.676 --> 00:06:20.676
- Hey, guys.

00:06:22.018 --> 00:06:23.170
Hi.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.503
- Woah, so fast.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.940
(Wren shouts)

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:34.802
I just crashed upstairs.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:36.680
I don't know if my skill
level's up to flying next door

00:06:36.682 --> 00:06:37.566
but I'm gonna try it.

00:06:37.566 --> 00:06:40.226
And like you're grandfather says,

00:06:41.912 --> 00:06:43.357
- I haven't told any of
them that I'm gonna do this.

00:06:43.357 --> 00:06:45.537
So, let's go do some recon.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.220
- Hey, Wren.

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:52.479
- You show up unannounced and
you're not even gonna tell

00:06:52.479 --> 00:06:54.229
me what you're up to?

00:06:56.271 --> 00:06:58.777
(heavy drum music)

00:06:58.780 --> 00:06:59.820
(claps)

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.700
- Hey, here goes nothing.

00:07:04.804 --> 00:07:08.190
(drone buzzes)

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.070
(heavy drum music)

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.380
- It's a great start.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.533
- I'm next door.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:13.893
I'm next door.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.091
Hey, everyone.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.700
- Are they totally freaking out right now?

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.807
(mumbles)

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.137
(heavy drum music)

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.267
(classic music)

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.715
- Hey, I'm trapped!

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.773
They put me in prison.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:48.851
- You know the real test is if
you can go say hi to Brandon.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.900
(suspenseful music)

00:08:04.216 --> 00:08:06.283
- All right, I'm in sixth.

00:08:06.283 --> 00:08:09.283
(suspenseful music)

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.813
No, he's trying to shoot me.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.272
Oh, dang it!

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.313
No!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.182
I'm upside down.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.074
Please return me to my glory.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.595
No, it's Kevin.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:51.994
It's Kevin.

00:08:52.148 --> 00:08:52.981
No!

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:56.733
No!

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:58.660
God, I'm trapped in a prison.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:08:59.640
This is probably Kevin's doing.

00:08:59.840 --> 00:09:01.146
There you are!

00:09:01.566 --> 00:09:03.206
(suspenseful music)

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:06.458
Why you do this?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.928
And that my friend is how
you mess with other studios.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:11.414
- Dude, you got them good.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.412
- Yeah, I did until they
trapped me in a hat prison.

00:09:14.412 --> 00:09:15.497
I didn't expect that.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.020
I should have in hindsight.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.072
- Now, if they put a stink
bomb on and you're gonna

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.044
drop it on them.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.617
- Dude, stink bomb status?

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.724
- Middle school status?

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.006
(Wren laughs)

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.934
- I call that a success, Nick!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.459
It took us more than a day.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:33.195
But we got to it in the end.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.469
- Thanks, grandpa.

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.153
- Yeah, thanks, grandpa.

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.013
(high fives)

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:38.600
Hereditary high five.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:42.240
(drone buzzes)

00:09:46.340 --> 00:09:49.007
(electro music)

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.432
He's driving down the thing right now.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:53.333
- Where?

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:55.510
Where is he?

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:56.562
- Holy (beep).

00:09:56.562 --> 00:09:58.614
- Oh, there he is.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.040
- Holy (beep).

